# Patterns excluded when the chart is packaged.
#
# Two things worth knowing before adding to this file, because both are easy to get wrong and
# neither fails loudly:
#
#   1. `.helmignore` also filters `.Files`. A template that reads a file through `.Files.Get` or
#      `.Files.Glob` sees nothing if that path is ignored — so `rules/` and `dashboards/`, which
#      are loaded into the PrometheusRule and the dashboard ConfigMap at render time, must never
#      appear here. They would not error; the objects would simply come out empty.
#   2. Everything below is development-time material that nothing reads at install or upgrade
#      time. Shipping it makes every published package larger and invites the assumption that a
#      chart's tests are part of its contract.

# Version control and editor droppings
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
.project
.settings/

# Test material. `helm unittest`, `ct` and `.github/scripts/test-rules.sh` all read these from the
# working tree, never from a packaged chart.
tests/
ci/
rules-tests/

# helm-docs input. `README.md` is generated from it and is what a consumer reads.
README.md.gotmpl

# Configuration contracts. `config-contract.yaml` declares what this chart's rendered
# configuration must satisfy and `contracts/` vendors the documents its images publish; both are
# read from the working tree by `just check-config`, never at install or upgrade time.
config-contract.yaml
contracts/
